<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Una (river)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Una is a river of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>, a right tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sava">Sava</a>, which for much of its course forms the border between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herzegovina">Herzegovina</a>. It flows past <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihac">Bihać</a> and is known for its clear water and waterfalls, protected in Una National Park. In antiquity its valley was home to the Iapydes.</p></div>
